      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$\\angle CBA=\\sin^{-1}(\\frac{7}{8})=1.0654$ radians, or $\\angle CBD=\\cos^{-1}(-\\frac{17}{32})=2.13$ radians. — B1. Accept $61.0^\\circ$, $66^\\circ$ or $122^\\circ$.\nSector $BCYD=\\frac12\\times8^2\\times2\\times\\text{their }1.0654=68.19$, or sector $CBY=\\frac12\\times8^2\\times\\text{their }1.0654$ (similarly sector $DBY$). — M1. Angle must be in radians; an equivalent degrees method is acceptable.\n$\\triangle BCD=7\\sqrt{8^2-7^2}$, or $\\frac12\\times8^2\\sin(2\\times\\text{their }1.0654)=27.11$. — M1. Award for triangle $ABC$ or $ABD$.\nSemicircle $CXD=\\frac12\\pi\\times7^2=76.97$. — M1. M1M1 for segment area formula used correctly.\nTotal area $=\\text{their }68.19-\\text{their }27.11+\\text{their }76.97=118.0$ to $118.1$. — M1A1. The M1 cannot be gained without an attempt to find $\\angle CBA$ or $\\angle CBD$.\nTotal: 6",
